# Given: a deterministic envelope of a Korean name
# When: the decrypted value is filtered with native LIKE
1	1	1	0	utf8mb4
# Then: infix/prefix/suffix hit, non-match misses, charset is utf8mb4 (above)
# Scenario 2 — Given: a Latin name encrypted deterministically
# When: filtered case-insensitively through the default collation
1	1	utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci
# Then: both match — MySQL collation does the work, not C code (above)
# Scenario 3 — Given: a table of encrypted Korean names
# When: the server searches for the partial match %길%
2
3
# Then: rows 2 and 3 match server-side, no rows shipped to the client (above)
